# Expected (line, col, len, role) for union.id. HAND-WRITTEN from the law.
#
# THIS FIXTURE IS A CONTROL, and it is the one span gaps/GAP-078.md's ruling
# does NOT reach. `|` has three meanings and only two hues. In shape space —
# reached through `shapedecl -> name ":" shape` — it is the orange `union`
# edge and is decidable, which is line 2. Outside it, §0g reads `|` as a PIPE
# ("channels = stream places composed by `|`", green) and pass100 §4 reads it
# as `bor` over integer operands, which no hue names at all.
#
# Line 3 is `out = xs | ys`. Nothing on it opens a stream place, so both
# readings stand and the projector DIAGNOSES rather than defaulting to green.
# The one surface fact that does separate them is a world action opening the
# line — `sh "ls" | grep("duo")` is a pipe because `sh` opened a stream — and
# that is what `fixtures/highlight/duon/union.id` asserts on the other side.
#
# Do NOT green this by widening the projector. The repair is a rule saying
# which reading wins over ordinary operands, and there is no such rule in the
# law today. A gate that reports "0 unresolved spans" over a corpus that
# cannot produce one is the kind of zero §3 calls a broken gate; this row is
# what stops that here. # gap[078]
spans = {
    { 1, 1, 8, "comment" },
    { 2, 1, 1, "place" },
    { 2, 2, 1, "copula" },
    { 2, 4, 3, "descriptor" },
